assistant line=26 text=The shared contract is now in force. One key consequence is that I’ll treat any proof-only rewrite that skips program execution as suspect unless it has a bridge-free universal connection proof; concrete examples alone cannot justify it. I’m also preserving the fixed supplied semantics rather than cloning or modifying it.
assistant line=50 text=The task is the balanced-parenthesis group splitter. I’m using a single left-to-right scanner that ignores spaces, tracks nesting depth, accumulates the current group, and appends exactly when the depth returns to zero. This stays within the supplied AST/K subset: plain assignments, a `for`, integer/string operations, conditionals, and `list.append`.
